proof.text:
Combining Steps 3, 5, 6 and 9 gives
$$s\text{ is horn-}p\text{-Cartesian}
\iff\phi\text{ is trivial Kan}
\iff(\forall z,\ \phi_z\text{ is a weak equivalence})
\iff(\forall z,\ \text{the stated postcomposition square is a homotopy pullback}).$$
Each test vertex is a vertex of $E$, with no restriction on its image in $B$. Every construction involved only the given edge, inner-horn fillers, and the cited fiber and path-space results. Hence no existence of other Cartesian lifts, and no Cartesian-fibration hypothesis on $p$, has entered either implication.
